[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4872811096","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4872811096","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4872811096,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABInEyWA","user":{"login":"Nintorch","id":92302738,"node_id":"U_kgDOBYBtkg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/92302738?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch","html_url":"https://github.com/Nintorch","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nintorch/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T05:14:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T05:14:06Z","body":"- I'm afraid this PR basically reverts https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/119329, and that would reopen https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/119320 :(","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4872811096/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4873804586","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4873804586","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4873804586,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIoBbKg","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T07:27:20Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T07:27:20Z","body":"@Nintorch I tested it but can't reproduce that regression.\r\nTested on Fedora linux and Android.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4873804586/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4877139565","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4877139565","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4877139565,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIrM-bQ","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T14:14:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T14:15:51Z","body":"> This also begs the question: should we really ignore emulated events altogether in `BaseButton`? Could there be a project that relies on `BaseButton` reacting to artificial `InputEventMouseButton` and `InputEventMouseMotion` events generated by the game code?\r\n\r\nAccording to [implementation](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/master/core/input/input.cpp#L863), if `emulate_mouse_from_touch` is true, every touch input generates a corresponding mouse event. Likewise, if `emulate_touch_from_mouse` is true, every mouse input generates a corresponding touch event. So, we do need to ignore one event.\r\n\r\nThe same logic also applies when the user calls `Input.parse_input_event(...)` from game code and these calls are not marked as emulated, unless user manually sets the `event.device = InputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION`.\r\n\r\nSo, if the event's device is explicitly set to `InputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION`, in that case it would now be ignored. However, there's little to no reason for users to even set `device` in the first place. This is the only case that is breaking.\r\nI think the solution here would be to document that `InputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION` should only be used for checking the physical input and not be used with `Input.parse_input_event(...)` to set device id and mention this in 4.7 migration guide?\r\n\r\nInputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION [class reference](https://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/classes/class_inputevent.html#class-inputevent-constant-device-id-emulation) already makes it very clear that it's only for checking physical input.\r\n\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4877139565/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4877254715","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4877254715","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4877254715,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIrUAOw","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-03T14:29:35Z","updated_at":"2026-07-03T14:29:35Z","body":"This also needs to be cherrypicked to 4.7, and `breaks compat` and `cherrypick` don't usually go together. I think it's probably fine in this case since the behavior change is very minor?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4877254715/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4883016254","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4883016254","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4883016254,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIwzqPg","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-04T16:14:47Z","updated_at":"2026-07-04T16:14:47Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4883016254/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4883131000","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4883131000","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4883131000,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIw6qeA","user":{"login":"KurodaKayn","id":146511017,"node_id":"U_kgDOCLuUqQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146511017?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn","html_url":"https://github.com/KurodaKayn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-04T16:54:34Z","updated_at":"2026-07-04T16:54:34Z","body":"I still think this fix is too broad and not precise enough.\r\n\r\nReturning early for every `InputEvent::DEVICE_ID_EMULATION` event means `BaseButton` now ignores more than just mouse events generated from touch input. This can also block:\r\n\r\n- User-created `InputEventMouseButton` events if the script sets `device = InputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION`.\r\n- Other emulated mouse events that are not generated from touch input.\r\n- Any future synthetic input path that reuses `DEVICE_ID_EMULATION`.\r\n\r\nThe bug here is specifically about the duplicated mouse event generated from touch input, so I think the fix should distinguish that source instead of treating all emulated events as equivalent.\r\n\r\nWhy not use the more precise approach from my PR? It marks mouse events generated from touch input and makes `BaseButton` ignore only those. Without the tests, the actual implementation is still under 30 lines, and it avoids changing the behavior of unrelated emulated mouse input.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4883131000/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4883418429","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4883418429","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4883418429,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIxMNPQ","user":{"login":"ace24713","id":753186,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc1MzE4Ng==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/753186?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713","html_url":"https://github.com/ace24713","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ace24713/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-04T18:36:32Z","updated_at":"2026-07-04T18:36:32Z","body":"Has anyone tested how this interacts with a button_mask set to right click and/or the project setting enable_long_press_as_right_click?","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4883418429/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4885622161","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4885622161","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4885622161,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIzStkQ","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T10:03:31Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T10:03:31Z","body":"> I still think this fix is too broad and not precise enough.\r\n> \r\n> Returning early for every `InputEvent::DEVICE_ID_EMULATION` event means `BaseButton` now ignores more than just mouse events generated from touch input. This can also block:\r\n> \r\n> * User-created `InputEventMouseButton` events if the script sets `device = InputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION`.\r\n\r\nYes, but it is documented that DEVICE_ID_EMULATION is used for `touch to mouse` and `mouse to touch` emulation. I'd expect users to not set this in the first place. Anyway, I'll mention this compact break in 4.7 migration guide.\r\n\r\n> * Other emulated mouse events that are not generated from touch input.\r\n\r\nThe only other emulated event is for `mouse to touch`, and that will have a corresponding mouse event, so it will be handled too.\r\n\r\n> * Any future synthetic input path that reuses `DEVICE_ID_EMULATION`.\r\n\r\nAs I said, DEVICE_ID_EMULATION is documented that it's for touch-mouse emulation, so I'd say it shouldn't be resued for any other purpose.\r\n\r\n> The bug here is specifically about the duplicated mouse event generated from touch input, so I think the fix should distinguish that source instead of treating all emulated events as equivalent.\r\n> \r\n> Why not use the more precise approach from my PR? It marks mouse events generated from touch input and makes `BaseButton` ignore only those. Without the tests, the actual implementation is still under 30 lines, and it avoids changing the behavior of unrelated emulated mouse input.\r\n\r\nYour PR is essentially doing the same thing. Instead of returning early, it ntroduces a new property and add checks for emulated events.\r\n","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4885622161/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4885629180","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4885629180","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4885629180,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIzTI_A","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T10:06:19Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T11:37:50Z","body":"> Has anyone tested how this interacts with a button_mask set to right click and/or the project setting enable_long_press_as_right_click?\r\n\r\nTouch events don't have a button mask, so this has no effect on touch input. However, if you have encountered unexpected behavior, please open a bug report.\r\n\r\nEdit: tested with `enable_long_press_as_right_click`, there's a bug i found https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120962","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4885629180/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4886497842","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4886497842","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4886497842,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0IKMg","user":{"login":"KurodaKayn","id":146511017,"node_id":"U_kgDOCLuUqQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/146511017?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn","html_url":"https://github.com/KurodaKayn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/KurodaKayn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T15:06:41Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T15:06:41Z","body":"> Your PR is essentially doing the same thing. Instead of returning early, it ntroduces a new property and add checks for emulated events.\r\n\r\nSmall correction: my PR does not check for emulated events in general.\r\n\r\nIt checks for mouse events specifically generated from touch input. \r\n`DEVICE_ID_EMULATION` remains broader: touch->mouse, mouse->touch, and user-dispatched events using that device id.\r\n\r\nSo difference is not early return vs extra property. Difference is device-wide filtering vs source-specific filtering.\r\n\r\nI see your point about `DEVICE_ID_EMULATION` being documented for touch-mouse emulation.\r\n\r\nMy concern is where policy is applied. Returning early in `BaseButton` makes `DEVICE_ID_EMULATION` mean “Button must ignore this event”. Docs say it identifies emulated input, not that GUI controls should drop it.\r\n\r\nThat also creates a compat break for user-dispatched `InputEventMouseButton` with `device = DEVICE_ID_EMULATION`. If this needs migration guide mention, then behavior change is real.\r\n\r\nI don’t think my PR does same thing. It only marks mouse events generated from touch input, then `BaseButton` ignores only that duplicate mouse path. Regular emulated mouse events still work.\r\n\r\nBug is specifically “real touch + generated mouse both handled”. So fix can suppress only generated mouse sibling, not all emulated input.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4886497842/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4886617597","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-4886617597","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":4886617597,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABI0Pd_Q","user":{"login":"syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247","html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-05T15:47:27Z","updated_at":"2026-07-05T15:47:27Z","body":"> That also creates a compat break for user-dispatched `InputEventMouseButton` with `device = DEVICE_ID_EMULATION`. If this needs migration guide mention, then behavior change is real.\r\n\r\nThis compact break is intentional and I think this is only issue. If there's any other behaviour change that you observed then please create a bug report for that.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4886617597/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5269169964","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/120864#issuecomment-5269169964","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120864","id":5269169964,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABOhEnLA","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.co